3.1 Clinical Evaluation Metrics Framework
To assess performance, we measure diagnostic capabilities across multiple metrics [@fawcett2006introduction; @steyerberg2010assessing]:

Sensitivity (Recall / True Positive Rate): Proportion of true stroke patients flagged by the model: \text{Sensitivity} = \frac{TP}{TP + FN}
Specificity (True Negative Rate): Proportion of healthy patients correctly identified as negative: \text{Specificity} = \frac{TN}{TN + FP}
Positive Predictive Value (PPV / Precision): Probability that a positive test indicates a true stroke event: \text{PPV} = \frac{TP}{TP + FP}
Balanced Accuracy: Average of sensitivity and specificity, resistant to class prevalence shifts: \text{Balanced Accuracy} = \frac{\text{Sensitivity} + \text{Specificity}}{2}
Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC-ROC): Rank-order discrimination across all possible decision cutoffs.
